    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26873" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lixīvus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>made into lye</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cinis lixiva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Larg. 216</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">230</span></i>; Varr. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				36, 27, 69, § 202</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15, 17, 18, §
			67</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mustum lixivum,</span>”
				<i>the must which flows from the grapes before they are
						pressed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lixīvum</span></b> , i, n., <i>lye</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall. 2, 15,
			18</span></i>; and so perh. <i><span class="en">Col. 12, 50, 11</span></i>.</div>
